    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4468cfeb-f9fa-52f4-8e7f-96e11f126dbc" activityNameId="bb32e4da-6d89-5a05-b539-a1876ce5e346" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Scantling, softwood, laminated, FFF, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Scantling, softwood, laminated, FFF, at plant
The thickness of the scantling is 0.071m. The bill of materials is based on data from two scantling producers. Allocation of co-products is either based on physical properties (wood inputs) or economical properties (working materials, production loss). An unweighted average was calculated.;
UUID: 158475d3-38a5-3d67-8853-96dbf6687199
Included are the materials used in a laminated (F=finger-jointed) scantling. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at scantling producers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_158475d3-38a5-3d67-8853-96dbf6687199.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
